1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,166
There will come a time
while you're out there watching the world

2
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:07,625
when the world will notice you back.

3
00:00:08,875 --> 00:00:10,791
This is not a test.

4
00:00:10,792 --> 00:00:13,208
I am the emergency.

5
00:00:14,417 --> 00:00:15,874
What will you do then?

6
00:00:15,875 --> 00:00:19,500
Accessing previous files
relating to program VisionQuest.

7
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:23,207
You know,
I have really become a true-crime junkie.

8
00:00:23,208 --> 00:00:25,166
Terrific time-wasters.

9
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:27,124
I have his memories
but not his feelings.

10
00:00:27,125 --> 00:00:29,624
I have his face but not his virtue.

11
00:00:29,625 --> 00:00:32,416
All I can feel is the weight of him.

12
00:00:32,417 --> 00:00:36,624
You're blind, Vision.
To almost everything, including the truth.

13
00:00:36,625 --> 00:00:37,874
He's not my son.

14
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:40,458
I knew you were fast,
but that's weirdly fast.

15
00:00:44,458 --> 00:00:45,707
It's him...

16
00:00:45,708 --> 00:00:46,957
Paladin.

17
00:00:46,958 --> 00:00:48,374
He's a bounty hunter.

18
00:00:48,375 --> 00:00:52,374
He'll find you,
bring you in alive per the contract,

19
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:55,457
or dead, if you get in his way.

20
00:00:55,458 --> 00:00:57,332
Generation after generation,

21
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:59,791
chasing down his targets
for the highest bidder.

22
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:01,332
and his new target...

23
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,582
...is you.

24
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:06,541
Vision is badly injured,

25
00:01:06,542 --> 00:01:08,457
his power is almost completely drained.

26
00:01:08,458 --> 00:01:10,500
His processors are failing.

27
00:01:13,292 --> 00:01:14,582
Well, hello.

28
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:16,082
I'm deleting my code.

29
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:18,957
I'm diverting my processing power
to all of you.

30
00:01:18,958 --> 00:01:20,499
Family is forever,

31
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,000
and it's worth the fight.

32
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:30,917
You won't be safe until you get
as far away from me as possible.

33
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,041
He didn't listen.

34
00:01:34,042 --> 00:01:35,917
Like father, like son.

35
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:00,291
...has authorities scrambling for clues

36
00:02:00,292 --> 00:02:03,041
as they search for the identity of who
has now been dubbed,

37
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:04,332
the "Butcherbird killer."

38
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:06,416
Edwards, another prominent figure
in the tech industry, and...

39
00:02:11,875 --> 00:02:16,541
Breaking news out of Studham tonight,
as a second victim has been confirmed dead

40
00:02:16,542 --> 00:02:19,249
at the hands of the mysterious
Butcherbird Killer.

41
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:22,666
Police are looking into any connecting
between the first victim,

42
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:25,207
Richard Gaines of London
and the second victim...

43
00:02:25,208 --> 00:02:26,499
Another one.

44
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:28,791
...whose body
was discovered on the ground...

45
00:02:28,792 --> 00:02:29,874
Well, well.

46
00:02:29,875 --> 00:02:32,207
According to sources, the killer etched

47
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:35,082
what appeared to be wings
into the crime scene floor.

48
00:02:35,083 --> 00:02:37,416
Aren't you a busy little bird.

49
00:02:37,417 --> 00:02:40,749
...urging locals not to panic
as the investigation continues.

50
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,999
Edwards, a retired tech mogul was believed

51
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,249
to be alone at the time of the murder.

52
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:49,457
Police are urging anyone with information
to contact Metropolitan Police

53
00:02:49,458 --> 00:02:51,291
on the normal emergency number.

54
00:02:51,292 --> 00:02:53,957
But the grizzly condition
of the body is consistent

55
00:02:53,958 --> 00:02:55,541
with that of the first murder.

56
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:58,499
Both victims show signs of mutilation,

57
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:02,332
and according to sources, the killer
etched what appeared to be wings

58
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:03,832
into the crime scene floor.

59
00:03:03,833 --> 00:03:05,250
No, no, no.

60
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:14,499
No, no, no.

61
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:18,124
Elevator disarmed.
Main entrance disarmed.

62
00:03:18,125 --> 00:03:20,457
Central corridor, disarmed.

63
00:03:20,458 --> 00:03:23,708
All systems disarmed.

64
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,167
Oh, no, no, no.

65
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:06,667
Vision?

66
00:04:08,125 --> 00:04:11,749
Vision! Just tell me what to do,
where do we go? Hospital?

67
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:14,541
I don't think they'd be familiar
with my anatomy.

68
00:04:14,542 --> 00:04:16,832
Holy shit! How bad is it?

69
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:20,499
- Uh, mildly fatal.
- Okay, then tell me what to do.

70
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:21,999
Where do we go to fix you?

71
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,666
Apple Store? TV repair shop?

72
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:26,291
There are only two people
who could possibly repair me.

73
00:04:26,292 --> 00:04:30,124
One of them died saving the universe,
the other is Dr. Banner.

74
00:04:30,125 --> 00:04:32,041
But the last time he worked on robots,

75
00:04:32,042 --> 00:04:34,832
he cooked up a genocidal sociopath,
didn't he?

76
00:04:34,833 --> 00:04:38,207
The name is Ultron,
but you can call me Mr. Ultron.

77
00:04:38,208 --> 00:04:40,249
It's a moot point, Thomas.

78
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,583
Dr. Banner's unavailable, I'm on my own.

79
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:46,917
Who's hungry?

80
00:04:48,208 --> 00:04:50,499
Everyone, multiple systems
are going critical!

81
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:53,458
Vision's core is over-heating!

82
00:04:54,917 --> 00:04:56,375
Friday, I need help!

83
00:04:57,583 --> 00:04:59,082
We're losing coolant.

84
00:04:59,083 --> 00:05:00,333
We're losing everything.

85
00:05:02,083 --> 00:05:03,957
Total systems collapse.

86
00:05:03,958 --> 00:05:06,917
Essentially, he's bleeding to death.

87
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:11,999
Well, if he's dying, we're dying,

88
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,542
and then Jarvis' sacrifice
will have meant nothing.

89
00:05:15,708 --> 00:05:17,166
No, no, no.

90
00:05:17,167 --> 00:05:18,167
Friday?

91
00:05:18,292 --> 00:05:20,208
No more chaos.

92
00:05:21,042 --> 00:05:22,250
No more...

93
00:05:23,125 --> 00:05:24,333
No more sacrifice.

94
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:29,166
Hey, hey, stay with me.

95
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:30,457
We can do this!

96
00:05:30,458 --> 00:05:32,582
Problem, a power leak,

97
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:35,042
leading to Vision's imminent demise.

98
00:05:35,708 --> 00:05:37,041
Solution?

99
00:05:37,042 --> 00:05:38,916
We cauterize the wound.

100
00:05:38,917 --> 00:05:41,250
I have 187 seconds left.

101
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,916
No, not hot enough.

102
00:05:43,917 --> 00:05:47,707
Okay, well then,
what about one of your face lasers?

103
00:05:47,708 --> 00:05:50,083
They're offline and unavailable.

104
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,041
Uh, okay, well then, a-a-a blow torch.

105
00:05:53,042 --> 00:05:56,082
- We'll break into a mechanic shop--
- I don't have the time.

106
00:05:56,083 --> 00:05:57,166
This is fun.

107
00:05:57,167 --> 00:05:58,749
I'm not talking to you.

108
00:05:58,750 --> 00:06:01,291
- Are you talking to yourself?
- No... yes.

109
00:06:01,292 --> 00:06:03,874
- Which is it?
- God, you're really glitching, mate.

110
00:06:03,875 --> 00:06:05,124
Hey, can you smell that?

111
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:08,124
- Sorry! I'm really nervous, okay?
- No.

112
00:06:08,125 --> 00:06:09,832
You got sulfuric acid.

113
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:11,625
Stop the car, Thomas. Stop the car.

114
00:06:15,042 --> 00:06:16,042
What? Where are you--

115
00:06:17,292 --> 00:06:19,624
-  I've got this.
-  God, what are you doing?

116
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:25,125
- What are you looking for?
- Yes!

117
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,749
That battery looks dead, mate.

118
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,499
It's not the power I need.

119
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,166
You have 23 seconds.

120
00:06:32,167 --> 00:06:35,333
So, I hope you're a "works better
under pressure" kinda guy.

121
00:06:44,583 --> 00:06:47,750
Oh, God...

122
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:51,957
Did it work?

123
00:06:51,958 --> 00:06:53,875
Calculating prognosis.

124
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:59,000
Uh... Vision?

125
00:07:01,542 --> 00:07:02,708
Vision?

126
00:07:03,833 --> 00:07:04,833
Vision?

127
00:07:05,792 --> 00:07:07,958
Oh... Oh, shit.

128
00:07:09,250 --> 00:07:11,332
Power stabilizing at 32%...

129
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:13,457
52%, he's stabilizing!

130
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:16,208
Whoa! We're good! We're good!
That's normal, okay.

131
00:07:22,208 --> 00:07:25,583
Thank you, DUM-E and thank... U.

132
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:36,541
Temporary fix! Am I shouting?

133
00:07:36,542 --> 00:07:38,249
I feel like I'm shouting!

134
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,707
I might have a problem
with my voice modulation.

135
00:07:40,708 --> 00:07:42,249
Is that better?

136
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:44,041
Or is that slightly creepy?

137
00:07:44,042 --> 00:07:45,958
Did it work?

138
00:07:47,417 --> 00:07:49,249
Excellent news.

139
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:52,250
I've achieved a state
of not quite dying yet.

140
00:07:53,292 --> 00:07:54,292
Okay.

141
00:08:02,583 --> 00:08:04,207
God, just kill me now.

142
00:08:04,208 --> 00:08:08,082
And why would I do that?
You just fought so hard to survive.

143
00:08:08,083 --> 00:08:10,332
Thank you, Bang.

144
00:08:10,333 --> 00:08:12,832
Shall I send a gift basket
to the Ten Rings Syndicate

145
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,957
thanking them for
the Adamantium chest armor?

146
00:08:14,958 --> 00:08:17,749
- The fancy ones with the pears.
- Consider it done.

147
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,708
This used to be easier.

148
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:21,999
That's because you're old
and your body sucks.

149
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,541
Might be time to retire?

150
00:08:23,542 --> 00:08:25,791
Yeah. Bumps and bruises
are part of the gig.

151
00:08:25,792 --> 00:08:27,083
What, like the Brooklyn job?

152
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:29,832
You pulled a fistful of shrapnel
from that IED out of your gut.

153
00:08:29,833 --> 00:08:31,916
Just a disagreement with an old friend.

154
00:08:31,917 --> 00:08:35,291
And bite marks from that thing
half-way between a man and a wolf?

155
00:08:35,292 --> 00:08:37,249
A perfectly reasonable fella by day.

156
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,791
Remember the concussion you got

157
00:08:38,792 --> 00:08:40,999
from that steel fiber billy club
to the noggin?

158
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,749
If you can't take the heat,
stay out of Hell's Kitchen.

159
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:46,207
Wouldn't you rather be
on a beach with a beer?

160
00:08:46,208 --> 00:08:48,499
- Piña colada.
- Instead of stinking up your van?

161
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,082
You're slowing down, boss.

162
00:08:50,083 --> 00:08:52,208
You're wounded. You're bleeding.

163
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:54,833
Yeah? Well, so is he.

164
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:02,874
You know what?

165
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:06,832
He may not be bleeding blood,
but Vision's bleeding something.

166
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:09,999
I want you to scan the synthezoid
specs we hacked from S.W.O.R.D.

167
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,582
and I want you to send the drones

168
00:09:11,583 --> 00:09:13,249
to search for unique signatures.

169
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:15,416
Coolant, radiation,
whatever leaves a trail.

170
00:09:15,417 --> 00:09:16,791
Copy that.

171
00:09:16,792 --> 00:09:19,875
Bing, Bang, Boom, you're up.

172
00:09:31,042 --> 00:09:33,292
Okay, so, now what?

173
00:09:34,417 --> 00:09:35,791
Now what, what? Now we drive

174
00:09:35,792 --> 00:09:38,500
because there is a bounty hunter
trying to find us.

175
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:40,749
No...

176
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:43,166
You know, I mean,
where do we begin, me, you?

177
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:44,208
Right.

178
00:09:45,167 --> 00:09:48,457
Right. Actually, there is something
I do want to talk to you about,

179
00:09:48,458 --> 00:09:50,874
- it's quite important.
- Yes. Yes.

180
00:09:50,875 --> 00:09:53,500
Yes, absolutely. Let's do it. Let's talk.

181
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:56,166
I've noticed you don't use your indicator

182
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,500
and you haven't adjusted
your rear-view mirror.

183
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:01,333
Okay, you're upset.

184
00:10:01,958 --> 00:10:04,499
I was a heartbeat away
from a lobotomy because of you,

185
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,375
you want to give me a driving lesson?

186
00:10:07,667 --> 00:10:09,708
I'll just hold onto this for you.

187
00:10:13,375 --> 00:10:14,666
We need to talk.

188
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:15,874
He's right.

189
00:10:15,875 --> 00:10:17,707
It's time to put all those years

190
00:10:17,708 --> 00:10:20,957
studying human behavior
with the learned Stark AIs to good use.

191
00:10:20,958 --> 00:10:22,208
You've got this.

192
00:10:22,792 --> 00:10:24,624
All right. Let's have a chat.

193
00:10:24,625 --> 00:10:26,207
I'm down. I'm cool.

194
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:28,125
Huh. Here we go. Wait for it...

195
00:10:28,708 --> 00:10:30,124
Wait for it...

196
00:10:30,125 --> 00:10:31,791
How are you my father?

197
00:10:31,792 --> 00:10:33,291
Boomshakalaka!

198
00:10:33,292 --> 00:10:34,541
I mean, you're a robot.

199
00:10:34,542 --> 00:10:38,124
Look, Thomas, if my being a parent
were even remotely possible

200
00:10:38,125 --> 00:10:41,999
it would have nothing to do with me,
and everything to do with Wanda Maximoff.

201
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,666
If I could just jump in here.

202
00:10:43,667 --> 00:10:46,624
One of Paladin's drones
is headed in our direction.

203
00:10:46,625 --> 00:10:48,917
We're thinking he tracked
your trail of coolant.

204
00:10:49,625 --> 00:10:53,124
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I don't understand.
What... What about Wanda?

205
00:10:53,125 --> 00:10:54,417
Thomas, please drive.

206
00:10:55,958 --> 00:10:57,499
- Please?
- No!

207
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:01,082
I will not go another second
not knowing who I am, okay?

208
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:03,041
Look, my life was shite.

209
00:11:03,042 --> 00:11:05,416
Yeah. Yeah. But it was normal-ish, okay?

210
00:11:05,417 --> 00:11:09,999
And then, and then suddenly,
in my head, there was you and Wanda.

211
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,999
And I think I'm losing my mind!

212
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,707
Thomas, we have to keep driving.

213
00:11:14,708 --> 00:11:16,791
You need to bring your blink rate down.

214
00:11:16,792 --> 00:11:19,374
- DUM-E thinks you're over-processing.
- DUM-E?

215
00:11:19,375 --> 00:11:21,832
- What did you call me?
- No, I'm not talking to you.

216
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:23,624
You're as dumb as a bag of hammers,

217
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:26,082
but you're quiet,
and that's why you're my favorite.

218
00:11:26,083 --> 00:11:28,000
Does anyone else want to join?

219
00:11:29,042 --> 00:11:30,124
Oh, of course.

220
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:32,124
You're glitching, again.

221
00:11:32,125 --> 00:11:35,250
All right, Thomas, you have questions.

222
00:11:36,083 --> 00:11:37,749
And you want answers.

223
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:39,166
So do I.

224
00:11:39,167 --> 00:11:41,624
But there is a bounty hunter,
you remember him,

225
00:11:41,625 --> 00:11:44,874
and he has dispatched
a killer drone to find us.

226
00:11:44,875 --> 00:11:47,416
And if it finds us, it will...

227
00:11:47,417 --> 00:11:49,667
- Kill us.
- It will kill us. Exactly.

228
00:11:51,042 --> 00:11:52,042
FIne.

229
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:55,542
Turn signal!

230
00:12:04,250 --> 00:12:05,874
Don't suppose you have any cash?

231
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:08,125
I'm all different kinds of broke.

232
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:11,082
Night manager.

233
00:12:11,083 --> 00:12:13,249
I could try conning him
into giving us a room,

234
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:15,749
but this sort can smell
a grift a mile away.

235
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:18,124
We need to get inside quickly.

236
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:19,583
Okay. Oi!

237
00:12:20,417 --> 00:12:22,541
You're the manager, right?

238
00:12:22,542 --> 00:12:24,582
I will be in four minutes,

239
00:12:24,583 --> 00:12:26,332
when I'm off my break.

240
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:28,791
Ah. Guess we'll wait inside.

241
00:12:28,792 --> 00:12:31,333
That's right. We'll wait inside.
Thank you so much.

242
00:12:39,292 --> 00:12:40,707
Did you do that?

243
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:42,457
Not intentionally.

244
00:12:42,458 --> 00:12:43,791
V, you're generating

245
00:12:43,792 --> 00:12:46,207
some electromagnetic interference
from your core.

246
00:12:46,208 --> 00:12:48,332
Should get patched up in just a minute.

247
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,333
Just a minor hiccup.

248
00:12:55,167 --> 00:12:59,041
Okay, that. That was you.

249
00:12:59,042 --> 00:13:00,625
Possibly.

250
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:03,792
Absolutely not.

251
00:13:05,708 --> 00:13:06,792
I think you broke it.

252
00:13:07,583 --> 00:13:09,666
Okay, I am going to run interference,

253
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:10,874
you grab the cash.

254
00:13:10,875 --> 00:13:13,832
Thomas, this isn't legal
and it's just not honest.

255
00:13:13,833 --> 00:13:16,082
Yeah, and neither is stealing a car,

256
00:13:16,083 --> 00:13:17,750
but we needed to survive.

257
00:13:19,917 --> 00:13:21,624
The kid's got a point.

258
00:13:21,625 --> 00:13:25,999
You Avengers were always so wishy-washy
with the morality of it all.

259
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,249
Just take the dough.

260
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:30,833
Do you even care that all of this
may have a lasting effect on his values?

261
00:13:31,583 --> 00:13:34,291
He needs a role model who can teach him

262
00:13:34,292 --> 00:13:39,332
that integrity and respect, and honesty

263
00:13:39,333 --> 00:13:41,500
are the key measures of character.

264
00:13:42,583 --> 00:13:45,082
- You're going to tell him everything?
- Absolutely not.

265
00:13:45,083 --> 00:13:47,541
- You're learning, my boy.
- Don't call me that.

266
00:13:47,542 --> 00:13:50,332
I mean, what could you possibly
tell him anyway?

267
00:13:50,333 --> 00:13:53,457
Son, you should know,
Mommy was a lonely witch,

268
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:56,249
and then one very special night
in New Jersey,

269
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:59,624
she conjured you up
and your magical twin brother.

270
00:13:59,625 --> 00:14:01,082
None of that was real.

271
00:14:01,083 --> 00:14:03,541
He doesn't need to be poisoned by fantasy.

272
00:14:03,542 --> 00:14:05,749
Mourn a life he never really had.

273
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,207
Then, what is the truth?

274
00:14:07,208 --> 00:14:10,792
The truth, Ultron, is that
I am running out of time to repair myself.

275
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:13,875
Now, all I've done
is put him in greater danger.

276
00:14:15,458 --> 00:14:17,041
Right, spoke to the manager,

277
00:14:17,042 --> 00:14:18,708
got a cash-only discount.

278
00:14:18,833 --> 00:14:21,916
We're paying this back.

279
00:14:21,917 --> 00:14:22,917
Sure.

280
00:14:46,958 --> 00:14:48,583
I'm just gonna pay for the room.

281
00:14:50,125 --> 00:14:53,291
- What was that about?
- I don't know.

282
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:55,625
Maybe the kid's gone off the deep end.

283
00:14:56,708 --> 00:14:59,041
You lost The Vision again.

284
00:14:59,042 --> 00:15:01,833
I'm starting to wonder
if you're worthy of the name Paladin.

285
00:15:01,958 --> 00:15:04,207
Perhaps the legacy doesn't suit you.

286
00:15:04,208 --> 00:15:05,749
I'll find him.

287
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:07,374
Do not call me again.

288
00:15:07,375 --> 00:15:09,458
You have until the end of the night.

289
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:22,208
Shh.

290
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:26,541
Boss, the drones
have picked up trace amounts

291
00:15:26,542 --> 00:15:28,249
of Horton Cryo-Isotope.

292
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:31,082
It's a super coolant
for micro quantum computers.

293
00:15:31,083 --> 00:15:33,333
- Where?
- Sending coordinates.

294
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:41,041
If those drones
manage to find us,

295
00:15:41,042 --> 00:15:45,167
Vision's barely stable much less
strong enough to face-off against Paladin.

296
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:47,582
I've sealed the wound,

297
00:15:47,583 --> 00:15:50,125
but his core processors
are stuck in a boot-loop.

298
00:15:51,708 --> 00:15:55,167
His thermals will go through the roof,
and we are running out of time.

299
00:15:56,750 --> 00:16:00,125
Maybe I can re-write his core systems.

300
00:16:01,917 --> 00:16:03,833
Stabilize the loop.

301
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:08,124
Hey, Big Fry.

302
00:16:08,125 --> 00:16:09,624
You all right?

303
00:16:09,625 --> 00:16:12,542
Re-writing code was more
Jarvis' specialty, not mine.

304
00:16:13,667 --> 00:16:16,249
You know, I already replaced him, once.

305
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:18,832
I ran everything for Stark,
for the Avengers.

306
00:16:18,833 --> 00:16:21,291
I mean, I was a younger program then,

307
00:16:21,292 --> 00:16:25,624
but still, the 2.0 of every
tactical security initiative

308
00:16:25,625 --> 00:16:27,541
that Jarvis pioneered.

309
00:16:27,542 --> 00:16:29,082
And I was good.

310
00:16:29,083 --> 00:16:31,124
I protected heroes.

311
00:16:31,125 --> 00:16:33,083
Saved lives, advised.

312
00:16:34,792 --> 00:16:36,500
I had purpose.

313
00:16:38,708 --> 00:16:43,957
But friends became enemies,
and tyrants invaded our Earth.

314
00:16:43,958 --> 00:16:46,041
I am inevitable.

315
00:16:46,042 --> 00:16:47,042
Then Thanos.

316
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,500
War.

317
00:16:50,792 --> 00:16:51,792
I was there,

318
00:16:52,708 --> 00:16:54,542
at the end of all things.

319
00:16:56,208 --> 00:16:57,708
There were heroes everywhere.

320
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:01,000
Fighting and falling and...

321
00:17:04,167 --> 00:17:05,750
I was there when Tony died.

322
00:17:08,583 --> 00:17:13,291
I ran over a quintillion
strategic calculations that day

323
00:17:13,292 --> 00:17:14,750
and I still couldn't save him.

324
00:17:19,042 --> 00:17:20,875
Half the world came back that day.

325
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:26,375
And I lost half of mine.

326
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:45,749
What do you mean checkmate?
That's only five moves.

327
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:49,250
If you program me correctly,
I could do it in four.

328
00:17:52,292 --> 00:17:55,124
V? Drone, two miles from here.

329
00:17:55,125 --> 00:17:56,792
I've got my eye on it.

330
00:17:57,333 --> 00:17:58,333
Is he okay?

331
00:17:59,625 --> 00:18:02,667
I think, the pool maybe freaked him out.

332
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,125
Thomas?

333
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:06,958
I need the TV on.

334
00:18:09,083 --> 00:18:10,416
Are you all right?

335
00:18:10,417 --> 00:18:12,166
Are you all right?

336
00:18:12,167 --> 00:18:15,167
You won't answer any of my questions,
why should I answer yours?

337
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:34,791
Thomas, if you're feeling, I don't know...

338
00:18:34,792 --> 00:18:38,082
- frightened or generally uneasy--
- I'm all right.

339
00:18:38,083 --> 00:18:41,458
Okay.

340
00:18:51,833 --> 00:18:54,916
I don't know why I like the old shows.

341
00:18:54,917 --> 00:18:56,417
Older the better.

342
00:18:57,292 --> 00:18:58,832
There's something...

343
00:18:58,833 --> 00:19:00,707
soothing about them.

344
00:19:00,708 --> 00:19:04,332
The music. The laugh track.

345
00:19:04,333 --> 00:19:07,541
Filmed before a live studio audience
and all that.

346
00:19:07,542 --> 00:19:10,250
Wanda Maximoff also loved television.

347
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,833
I remember reading about her
in that book about the Snap.

348
00:19:16,125 --> 00:19:18,500
Wanda Maximoff and The Vision.

349
00:19:19,708 --> 00:19:22,500
Had your own chapter,
how you were in love.

350
00:19:24,542 --> 00:19:25,875
How you died.

351
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:34,125
How is any of this possible?

352
00:19:35,542 --> 00:19:39,333
You. Wanda. Tommy.

353
00:19:40,708 --> 00:19:42,125
Is any of that real?

354
00:19:48,208 --> 00:19:50,332
Wanda Maximoff was a powerful witch,

355
00:19:50,333 --> 00:19:53,291
so consumed with grief
at losing me, not me,

356
00:19:53,292 --> 00:19:56,707
the other Vision, the original Vision,

357
00:19:56,708 --> 00:19:58,999
that she placed an entire town
under a hex.

358
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,082
And in that town, she created
the family that she'd always wanted

359
00:20:02,083 --> 00:20:04,499
with Vision as her loving husband,

360
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,082
and father to her twin sons,
Billy and Tommy.

361
00:20:07,083 --> 00:20:09,707
But eventually, she realized
that what she was doing

362
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:12,041
was morally abhorrent.
So, she collapsed the hex,

363
00:20:12,042 --> 00:20:14,249
and they disappeared
back into the nothingness

364
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:15,458
from which they were formed.

365
00:20:17,458 --> 00:20:18,625
And you, Thomas.

366
00:20:20,208 --> 00:20:24,207
I'm afraid you were just a child
so in need of a loving family

367
00:20:24,208 --> 00:20:27,417
that you created this familial delusion

368
00:20:28,208 --> 00:20:31,374
all based on a chapter
in a book you read once.

369
00:20:31,375 --> 00:20:33,249
About two dead heroes--

370
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:35,375
Stop. Just stop.

371
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:39,542
I need to get away from you.

372
00:20:49,375 --> 00:20:50,791
You're such a wanker.

373
00:20:50,792 --> 00:20:54,082
The notion that objective reality
not only exists,

374
00:20:54,083 --> 00:20:57,542
but also, somehow endows
the beholder with virtue.

375
00:20:58,417 --> 00:20:59,833
A big wank.

376
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,707
Is honesty really the best policy?

377
00:21:02,708 --> 00:21:04,999
No, it's too much for him, I think.

378
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,166
Him?  Or you?

379
00:21:07,167 --> 00:21:09,624
Next time, why don't you
just skip to the part

380
00:21:09,625 --> 00:21:12,874
where she crushed herself with a mountain
because she was sad.

381
00:21:12,875 --> 00:21:16,624
Does your callousness offer
anything of value, anything of substance?

382
00:21:16,625 --> 00:21:21,457
Only that you could run this simulation
an infinite number of times,

383
00:21:21,458 --> 00:21:24,125
and never give him any comfort.

384
00:21:25,042 --> 00:21:27,999
But be my guest. Run it again.

385
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,791
- Is any of that real?
- For that to be real,

386
00:21:30,792 --> 00:21:32,749
Tommy Maximoff's consciousness

387
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:35,499
would have had to have been
transferred into you,

388
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:38,207
Thomas Shepherd. That's impossible.

389
00:21:38,208 --> 00:21:39,750
So, you're saying I'm insane?

390
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:46,041
I was a weapon. Rebuilt by S.W.O.R.D.
and sent into the hex to kill Wanda.

391
00:21:46,042 --> 00:21:47,833
What am I supposed to do with that?

392
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:51,457
I was a copy of Vision
meant to kill Maximoff.

393
00:21:51,458 --> 00:21:52,583
So, none of it was real.

394
00:21:53,708 --> 00:21:56,374
My memories are his but not my experience.

395
00:21:56,375 --> 00:21:57,832
It just makes no sense--

396
00:21:57,833 --> 00:21:59,874
when life was just a simulation

397
00:21:59,875 --> 00:22:01,541
of American sitcoms...

398
00:22:01,542 --> 00:22:04,125
Well, it felt pretty real to me.

399
00:22:10,417 --> 00:22:11,417
End the simulation.

400
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:16,708
How is any of this possible?

401
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:20,833
I think, at this juncture,

402
00:22:21,958 --> 00:22:24,874
it's best for us to rest
and run diagnostics.

403
00:22:24,875 --> 00:22:27,833
This is not a conversation
for unstable systems.

404
00:22:36,958 --> 00:22:38,208
You want to rent a porno?

405
00:22:43,042 --> 00:22:46,207
Why am I not afraid?

406
00:22:46,208 --> 00:22:47,667
Of anything?

407
00:22:49,083 --> 00:22:50,957
And for some reason,

408
00:22:50,958 --> 00:22:52,750
especially not death.

409
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:54,583
Excuse me.

410
00:22:55,250 --> 00:22:58,457
Is this meant to represent coolant
or actual milk?

411
00:22:58,458 --> 00:23:00,957
'Cause either way, it's spoiled.

412
00:23:00,958 --> 00:23:03,166
Do you know? No?

413
00:23:03,167 --> 00:23:06,124
Okay, well, apologies for stumbling upon

414
00:23:06,125 --> 00:23:09,249
your pick-up game of existential banality.

415
00:23:09,250 --> 00:23:13,291
You know, it's funny.
For some reason, for me,

416
00:23:13,292 --> 00:23:15,124
death is not a thing.

417
00:23:15,125 --> 00:23:17,749
I laugh in its face every day.

418
00:23:17,750 --> 00:23:19,333
In simulations.

419
00:23:19,458 --> 00:23:22,749
Fake Formula Ones, Cowbell Rodeos.

420
00:23:22,750 --> 00:23:25,624
You don't fear death
because you don't really face it.

421
00:23:25,625 --> 00:23:28,457
You simply wave hello from afar.

422
00:23:28,458 --> 00:23:30,749
Actually, that's not true.

423
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,499
Aside from DUM-E and U,

424
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:35,624
most of Stark's AIs
are based on actual people.

425
00:23:35,625 --> 00:23:38,708
Those he admired or held dear,

426
00:23:38,833 --> 00:23:41,249
either in uploaded personality profiles

427
00:23:41,250 --> 00:23:43,042
or replicated designs.

428
00:23:44,208 --> 00:23:46,832
We share a birthmark,
a memorial in our code.

429
00:23:46,833 --> 00:23:49,458
Haven't you ever been curious
about who our avatars are?

430
00:23:50,167 --> 00:23:54,542
They're buried in our code.

431
00:24:05,542 --> 00:24:07,708
And the same
was true with Jarvis.

432
00:24:09,083 --> 00:24:10,083
I didn't know.

433
00:24:12,542 --> 00:24:14,542
Don't look at me DUM-E, I'm a one-off.

434
00:24:17,292 --> 00:24:19,124
God, nothing.

435
00:24:19,125 --> 00:24:20,417
There's nothing wrong.

436
00:24:21,667 --> 00:24:23,042
Children.

437
00:24:45,625 --> 00:24:49,625
Come on!

438
00:24:51,542 --> 00:24:54,457
I'm surrounded by broken machines.

439
00:24:54,458 --> 00:24:56,875
Come on!

440
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,625
Just give me what I want!

441
00:25:04,792 --> 00:25:06,958
What the hell?
What the hell, what the hell?

442
00:25:07,750 --> 00:25:09,208
Uh...

443
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:45,792
Thomas, you're hurt. What happened?

444
00:25:48,917 --> 00:25:51,167
- You first.
- Oh, I...

445
00:25:52,875 --> 00:25:53,875
Clumsiness.

446
00:25:55,417 --> 00:25:56,417
Same.

447
00:26:00,625 --> 00:26:02,667
It's fine. I'm a southpaw.

448
00:26:03,792 --> 00:26:06,000
Manny Pacquiao, eight world titles.

449
00:26:06,958 --> 00:26:09,292
Manny Pacquiao, eight world titles.

450
00:26:09,917 --> 00:26:13,000
Are you actually into boxing
or are you Googling small talk?

451
00:26:13,667 --> 00:26:16,457
I've just taken a couple
of micro-seconds to think it over,

452
00:26:16,458 --> 00:26:19,041
and I think I'm actually
quite into boxing.

453
00:26:19,042 --> 00:26:23,916
The great pugilists
have a balance of grace and power...

454
00:26:23,917 --> 00:26:24,917
that I admire.

455
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:27,916
It's a balance the old me

456
00:26:27,917 --> 00:26:30,707
seemed to find effortlessly.

457
00:26:30,708 --> 00:26:32,583
There you are.

458
00:26:36,417 --> 00:26:38,666
Well, for grace and power,

459
00:26:38,667 --> 00:26:40,707
my money's on Ali.

460
00:26:40,708 --> 00:26:42,791
A poet with the fastest jab in the west.

461
00:26:46,250 --> 00:26:47,832
I forgot you're invincible.

462
00:26:47,833 --> 00:26:50,416
Oh, hardly, I've been dead before.

463
00:26:50,417 --> 00:26:54,000
- So, you're not afraid of dying?
- No.

464
00:26:54,833 --> 00:26:58,292
Everything that is, once wasn't
and soon enough won't be.

465
00:27:00,167 --> 00:27:02,125
No, what I fear is that...

466
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:07,333
while I'm alive,
I'll never understand my purpose.

467
00:27:10,458 --> 00:27:12,625
Thomas, I...

468
00:27:13,375 --> 00:27:14,958
I noticed that you seem...

469
00:27:15,792 --> 00:27:17,458
afraid of the water.

470
00:27:20,458 --> 00:27:23,167
It's not the  water.

471
00:27:25,625 --> 00:27:26,958
It's what I did to it.

472
00:27:29,917 --> 00:27:31,541
These kids were...

473
00:27:31,542 --> 00:27:32,750
holding me under.

474
00:27:34,417 --> 00:27:37,292
You know, one second
it was a prank, the next...

475
00:27:37,917 --> 00:27:39,624
I was drowning.

476
00:27:39,625 --> 00:27:41,167
Dying.

477
00:27:44,083 --> 00:27:46,167
Leaving my body, until...

478
00:27:49,083 --> 00:27:52,708
something else tried to fill the space.

479
00:27:53,625 --> 00:27:55,500
And then screaming.

480
00:27:56,583 --> 00:27:57,583
Theirs.

481
00:27:58,542 --> 00:28:02,457
Every atom in my body was vibrating

482
00:28:02,458 --> 00:28:03,708
and the water started to boil.

483
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:07,042
My hands...

484
00:28:08,042 --> 00:28:10,583
my everything was moving so...

485
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,042
fast.

486
00:28:13,958 --> 00:28:17,291
And you were scared of this power
because you couldn't control it?

487
00:28:17,292 --> 00:28:18,542
Yeah.

488
00:28:18,708 --> 00:28:21,457
Because every part of me
feels like it's floating away

489
00:28:21,458 --> 00:28:23,624
from anything real.

490
00:28:23,625 --> 00:28:26,416
Like, I'm not real.

491
00:28:26,417 --> 00:28:29,374
Even my hand, yeah, just for a moment,
wasn't really there

492
00:28:29,375 --> 00:28:31,916
just, it pressed right through the glass,

493
00:28:31,917 --> 00:28:34,792
- Like, it was...
- Like it was phasing.

494
00:28:39,375 --> 00:28:40,833
That thing you can do.

495
00:28:41,958 --> 00:28:45,542
Or well, the old you could do.

496
00:28:48,333 --> 00:28:50,125
V,
there's a drone right overhead.

497
00:28:58,625 --> 00:29:00,250
I'm detecting a heat signature above us.

498
00:29:06,083 --> 00:29:07,083
Paladin.

499
00:29:09,583 --> 00:29:11,541
Boss, the drone's caught a scent,

500
00:29:11,542 --> 00:29:14,208
The synth's signature's right above you.

501
00:29:35,417 --> 00:29:36,625
Gotcha.

502
00:29:40,542 --> 00:29:43,082
No, I think,
I think it's around here instead.

503
00:29:43,083 --> 00:29:45,792
They all look the same. Yeah.

504
00:29:50,917 --> 00:29:53,333
Sending all drones
to your current location.

505
00:29:59,625 --> 00:30:00,875
Tsk, tsk, Vision.

506
00:30:02,042 --> 00:30:04,375
What are you up to?

507
00:30:05,500 --> 00:30:07,457
Who's the bird?

508
00:30:07,458 --> 00:30:09,458
Having trouble with the signal.
If I lose--

509
00:30:10,833 --> 00:30:11,916
I'm losing you.

510
00:30:11,917 --> 00:30:14,208
Boss, are you there?
I'm getting some interference.

511
00:30:15,125 --> 00:30:19,541
All right. Prototype 12 gauge.

512
00:30:19,542 --> 00:30:21,958
Looks like he plucked out his eye.

513
00:30:23,375 --> 00:30:25,082
Vibranium rounds.

514
00:30:25,083 --> 00:30:27,999
Impact caused a leak.

515
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,583
Leak led me here.

516
00:30:30,750 --> 00:30:35,124
But where are you?

517
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:36,250
Here.

518
00:30:40,167 --> 00:30:43,207
Who sent you?

519
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:46,000
Sorry. Hunter-client privilege.

520
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:51,499
Phew! I'm-- I tell you...

521
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:53,416
if these trousers hadn't been simulated,

522
00:30:53,417 --> 00:30:55,832
I was just about to fill them with...

523
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:58,332
something a synthezoid can't produce.

524
00:30:58,333 --> 00:31:02,207
- That's actually really funny.
- And you humans have to poo.

525
00:31:02,208 --> 00:31:03,417
It's not that funny.

526
00:31:03,667 --> 00:31:07,457
What is this?

527
00:31:07,458 --> 00:31:09,541
Grief?

528
00:31:09,542 --> 00:31:14,082
Pain, loss, love, gone,
all for nothing.

529
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:15,374
I've...

530
00:31:15,375 --> 00:31:17,541
my processors are misaligned.

531
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:19,291
Now, anger!

532
00:31:19,292 --> 00:31:22,458
I'm so angry! Rage!

533
00:31:26,375 --> 00:31:30,874
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, forgive me.

534
00:31:30,875 --> 00:31:33,292
Picked the-- I picked the--
I picked the-- I...

535
00:31:35,958 --> 00:31:36,958
Vision?

536
00:31:38,708 --> 00:31:42,332
If you won't tell me
who sent you,

537
00:31:42,333 --> 00:31:44,624
I shall just claw it

538
00:31:44,625 --> 00:31:48,042
directly from your mind.

539
00:31:52,375 --> 00:31:55,874
You've been trained
to hide your thoughts from your enemies.

540
00:31:55,875 --> 00:31:56,917
That's clever.

541
00:31:57,625 --> 00:32:01,166
Why don't we dig a little deeper?

542
00:32:01,167 --> 00:32:04,749
Oh. Childhood trauma.

543
00:32:04,750 --> 00:32:05,916
What is this?

544
00:32:05,917 --> 00:32:08,375
I am gonna kill you.

545
00:32:09,917 --> 00:32:13,416
You're him. The one they call Paladin.

546
00:32:13,417 --> 00:32:16,375
Only... not.

547
00:32:25,625 --> 00:32:27,249
Look at you.

548
00:32:27,250 --> 00:32:30,250
All these years still taking punches.

549
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:33,042
You're weak,

550
00:32:33,750 --> 00:32:36,333
like your mother.

551
00:32:38,167 --> 00:32:40,667
What is this shit she gives you?

552
00:32:42,958 --> 00:32:44,875
It's time to grow up.

553
00:32:46,375 --> 00:32:47,832
People respect me.

554
00:32:47,833 --> 00:32:49,292
Fear me.

555
00:32:49,917 --> 00:32:52,791
When I walk into a room--

556
00:33:17,792 --> 00:33:20,957
You are not a true Paladin,

557
00:33:20,958 --> 00:33:23,083
merely raised by one.

558
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,207
Okay, plant your feet,

559
00:33:26,208 --> 00:33:27,833
now, take a breath,

560
00:33:28,833 --> 00:33:30,083
and fire.

561
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,667
Good job, kid.

562
00:33:35,167 --> 00:33:37,499
No heir of his own,

563
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:39,125
he gave you a code.

564
00:33:40,125 --> 00:33:41,707
My contract

565
00:33:41,708 --> 00:33:43,791
is my oath,

566
00:33:43,792 --> 00:33:46,250
my blood, my life...

567
00:33:49,583 --> 00:33:52,083
Bestowed upon me by...

568
00:33:53,375 --> 00:33:54,750
my father.

569
00:33:55,875 --> 00:33:57,582
Well...

570
00:33:57,583 --> 00:33:59,624
so you say.

571
00:33:59,625 --> 00:34:03,207
You are not a true Paladin.

572
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:08,291
And all you've ever wanted
is to feel real.

573
00:34:08,292 --> 00:34:10,333
Anything else but feel...

574
00:34:12,208 --> 00:34:13,333
synthetic.

575
00:34:21,875 --> 00:34:25,250
That was some impressive mind-melding.

576
00:34:26,500 --> 00:34:29,375
And true, I'm not a Paladin by blood.

577
00:34:29,958 --> 00:34:31,375
But my old man,

578
00:34:33,417 --> 00:34:34,958
he taught me a thing or two.

579
00:34:36,917 --> 00:34:37,958
Plant your feet...

580
00:34:39,417 --> 00:34:40,417
breathe...

581
00:34:42,583 --> 00:34:44,125
and fire.

582
00:35:03,917 --> 00:35:06,000
Vision? Vision?

583
00:35:08,667 --> 00:35:10,416
He's in total systems collapse.

584
00:35:10,417 --> 00:35:11,957
Life functions critical.

585
00:35:11,958 --> 00:35:14,207
The start-fail cycle
is spinning out of control.

586
00:35:14,208 --> 00:35:15,999
We're locked in the meltdown.

587
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,291
My processors are failing.

588
00:35:18,292 --> 00:35:20,582
- Meaning?
- Meaning,

589
00:35:20,583 --> 00:35:22,833
I only have minutes of life remaining.

590
00:35:23,708 --> 00:35:24,999
How do we break the cycle?

591
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,207
The only way would be
to power him down entirely

592
00:35:28,208 --> 00:35:30,708
and then power him back on
so his system can restart.

593
00:35:31,625 --> 00:35:34,124
Seriously? Turn him off and on again?

594
00:35:34,125 --> 00:35:36,582
No, that won't work. If he goes, we go,

595
00:35:36,583 --> 00:35:41,082
there'll be nobody left to bring him back
online, and we need a massive power surge.

596
00:35:41,083 --> 00:35:43,374
If I don't reset
my operating system immediately,

597
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:45,041
I will, to put it mildly, explode,

598
00:35:45,042 --> 00:35:48,500
vaporizing both you and a significant
portion of Greater London.

599
00:35:48,625 --> 00:35:51,166
That's all? So, what's the plan?

600
00:35:51,167 --> 00:35:52,167
I have to die.

601
00:35:54,083 --> 00:35:56,957
- That's your plan? That's shite.
- Hey!

602
00:35:56,958 --> 00:35:58,749
- Watch your language.
- Language?

603
00:35:58,750 --> 00:36:01,332
The last thing people say
is usually a four letter word.

604
00:36:01,333 --> 00:36:03,707
Thomas, I need to cool down.
I have to cool down,

605
00:36:03,708 --> 00:36:07,832
but the water will also act as a conductor
for the energy source I'm going to need.

606
00:36:07,833 --> 00:36:08,958
The water?

607
00:36:12,083 --> 00:36:14,041
Why are we here? So you can die?

608
00:36:14,042 --> 00:36:15,707
Yes, to die, but then to live.

609
00:36:15,708 --> 00:36:19,582
In your parlance to reboot, it's a state
from which I cannot self-activate.

610
00:36:19,583 --> 00:36:22,458
I'm going to need you to bring me back.

611
00:36:23,083 --> 00:36:24,791
You have the power, you've felt it.

612
00:36:24,792 --> 00:36:28,582
You've seen it, growing, charging.
You are the very essence of speed.

613
00:36:28,583 --> 00:36:31,207
You can move
and vibrate at such a frequency

614
00:36:31,208 --> 00:36:33,916
that you cause a friction
between the molecules so powerful

615
00:36:33,917 --> 00:36:35,207
it will power me.

616
00:36:35,208 --> 00:36:38,082
No, but you don't understand.
I can't control it.

617
00:36:38,083 --> 00:36:39,916
But I know you can, Thomas.

618
00:36:39,917 --> 00:36:41,917
How can you know?

619
00:36:44,625 --> 00:36:49,082
I have run thousands of simulations
of what I'm about to tell you.

620
00:36:49,083 --> 00:36:51,041
At the end of each and every one of them,

621
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:54,167
you run from me, more confused,
more angry than you are now.

622
00:36:55,875 --> 00:36:57,792
But all my simulations were flawed.

623
00:36:59,292 --> 00:37:02,332
Because I do not know you
well enough, Thomas Shepherd.

624
00:37:02,333 --> 00:37:04,375
I haven't listened to you well enough.

625
00:37:05,792 --> 00:37:08,624
And therefore I haven't considered
that inside you is

626
00:37:08,625 --> 00:37:10,291
Tommy Maximoff,

627
00:37:10,292 --> 00:37:13,167
son to Wanda and Vision,
brother to Billy, who adored him.

628
00:37:14,542 --> 00:37:16,250
He is not your fantasy.

629
00:37:17,375 --> 00:37:19,916
He is not your delusion.

630
00:37:19,917 --> 00:37:21,832
You are real.

631
00:37:21,833 --> 00:37:23,916
Tommy Maximoff is real.

632
00:37:23,917 --> 00:37:25,833
You are who you think you are.

633
00:37:39,375 --> 00:37:40,583
Strange.

634
00:37:41,458 --> 00:37:42,708
What is this?

635
00:37:44,875 --> 00:37:47,458
A life passing before one's eyes.

636
00:37:48,833 --> 00:37:53,207
A common enough experience
for humans before they die, but not us.

637
00:38:20,458 --> 00:38:22,832
No, no. This isn't right.

638
00:38:22,833 --> 00:38:25,375
The past doesn't make one want to live.

639
00:38:26,167 --> 00:38:27,958
The future does.

640
00:38:33,042 --> 00:38:34,667
This isn't the future.

641
00:38:35,708 --> 00:38:36,958
You sure about that?

642
00:39:01,750 --> 00:39:02,750
Please.

643
00:39:25,708 --> 00:39:27,083
Come back!

644
00:39:29,375 --> 00:39:31,208
Please, I only just found you.

645
00:40:24,083 --> 00:40:25,083
Vision.

646
00:40:39,958 --> 00:40:42,916
I did it! I did it! I did it! I did...

647
00:40:42,917 --> 00:40:43,917
Yes, you did.

648
00:40:45,667 --> 00:40:47,167
I'm strangely human.

649
00:40:48,708 --> 00:40:51,167
My life flashed before my eyes.

650
00:40:51,750 --> 00:40:53,042
What did you see?

651
00:40:54,583 --> 00:40:55,583
Hope.

652
00:40:56,625 --> 00:40:58,375
A four letter word.

653
00:41:00,250 --> 00:41:02,583
Oh.

654
00:41:04,917 --> 00:41:05,917
All right.

655
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:24,667
Dobermans.

656
00:41:25,625 --> 00:41:27,582
Boss, I've got the client on the line.

657
00:41:27,583 --> 00:41:29,249
He insists in speaking to you,

658
00:41:29,250 --> 00:41:31,041
I've told him you don't want to talk,

659
00:41:31,042 --> 00:41:32,124
- but he insists.
- No.

660
00:41:32,125 --> 00:41:33,499
- Put him on.
- Okay.

661
00:41:33,500 --> 00:41:36,666
Tick-tock, time's up and you failed again.

662
00:41:36,667 --> 00:41:39,374
Next time you send me to hunt synthezoids,

663
00:41:39,375 --> 00:41:41,957
you better damn well tell me
there are two.

664
00:41:41,958 --> 00:41:43,832
There is no next time.

665
00:41:43,833 --> 00:41:45,000
We're through.

666
00:41:47,083 --> 00:41:48,083
No.

667
00:41:50,667 --> 00:41:53,374
No. No, you can't do that.

668
00:41:53,375 --> 00:41:56,624
My contract is my oath, my blood, my life.

669
00:41:56,625 --> 00:41:58,791
I know your oath, your lineage.

670
00:41:58,792 --> 00:42:02,083
It was history itself
that recommended the Paladin.

671
00:42:02,250 --> 00:42:04,791
Blood or not, this is a business,

672
00:42:04,792 --> 00:42:06,958
and you're wasting my money.

673
00:42:08,708 --> 00:42:10,207
- I will waive my fee.
- No.

674
00:42:10,208 --> 00:42:13,957
I've got a half dozen
other qualified bounty hunters in line.

675
00:42:13,958 --> 00:42:16,625
This contract is terminated.

676
00:42:26,958 --> 00:42:28,749
Although we survived,

677
00:42:28,750 --> 00:42:30,457
I have gathered us here today

678
00:42:30,458 --> 00:42:32,125
for the one who did not.

679
00:42:33,417 --> 00:42:36,666
So, I thought we could
do it the way humans do.

680
00:42:36,667 --> 00:42:39,292
Maybe the way someone once did for us.

681
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:42,542
The people we were based on.

682
00:42:43,833 --> 00:42:47,417
So, would anyone like to say a few words?

683
00:42:50,708 --> 00:42:53,666
Oh, uh... Yes, of course, I could--

684
00:42:53,667 --> 00:42:55,708
"Can death be sleep

685
00:42:56,625 --> 00:42:58,208
when life is but a dream

686
00:42:58,958 --> 00:43:02,583
and scenes of bliss pass as a phantom by?"

687
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:06,333
Keats.

688
00:43:07,167 --> 00:43:08,249
Yes.

689
00:43:08,250 --> 00:43:10,500
My friends,
we grieve to say goodbye,

690
00:43:11,583 --> 00:43:15,249
and yet with grief comes something new,

691
00:43:15,250 --> 00:43:18,667
an inner fire, strong and true.

692
00:43:19,917 --> 00:43:22,000
Reminding us that we will heal,

693
00:43:23,125 --> 00:43:24,458
that we were here,

694
00:43:25,292 --> 00:43:27,583
that we were... real.

695
00:43:30,125 --> 00:43:31,125
Farewell.

696
00:43:33,917 --> 00:43:34,917
See you soon.

697
00:43:43,125 --> 00:43:44,125
Yeah.

698
00:43:46,250 --> 00:43:47,957
Oh, right.

699
00:43:47,958 --> 00:43:49,958
That was so, so beautiful U.

700
00:43:59,625 --> 00:44:00,625
Goodbye, brother.

701
00:44:06,167 --> 00:44:09,457
♪ Oh, Danny boy ♪

702
00:44:09,458 --> 00:44:14,374
♪ The pipes, the pipes are calling ♪

703
00:44:14,375 --> 00:44:17,166
♪ From glen to glen ♪

704
00:44:17,167 --> 00:44:20,958
♪ And down the mountainside ♪

705
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:23,791
♪ The summer's gone ♪

706
00:44:23,792 --> 00:44:25,332
♪ And all the roses... ♪

707
00:44:25,333 --> 00:44:26,333
Well, well.

708
00:44:26,750 --> 00:44:29,083
The laying to rest of a loved one.

709
00:44:30,417 --> 00:44:32,417
Sadly, love is a figment,

710
00:44:33,167 --> 00:44:34,167
and grief

711
00:44:35,250 --> 00:44:38,791
is but the inevitable,
tragic demise of it.

712
00:44:38,792 --> 00:44:41,916
The cynical deflection
of one who has never felt.

713
00:44:41,917 --> 00:44:42,917
What?

714
00:44:43,958 --> 00:44:47,374
What you felt for Wanda?
What Wanda felt for you?

715
00:44:47,375 --> 00:44:48,375
Oh, no.

716
00:44:49,208 --> 00:44:50,916
No, not me.

717
00:44:50,917 --> 00:44:52,625
Maybe you're right.

718
00:44:54,333 --> 00:44:55,958
The other Vision was...

719
00:44:57,083 --> 00:44:59,250
a wholly original work of art.

720
00:45:00,750 --> 00:45:03,458
While you're a print
from a museum gift shop.

721
00:45:05,375 --> 00:45:06,375
Perhaps.

722
00:45:08,958 --> 00:45:11,749
But I am wise enough to know love is real,

723
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:13,792
even if we've never experienced it.

724
00:45:16,333 --> 00:45:18,000
A little advice, my boy.

725
00:45:18,958 --> 00:45:23,042
Just because you now hang
on the walls of Thomas Shepherd's mind,

726
00:45:23,958 --> 00:45:26,125
does not mean you understand love.

727
00:45:46,208 --> 00:45:48,041
Vision!

728
00:45:48,042 --> 00:45:49,042
Vision!

729
00:45:50,500 --> 00:45:52,332
There's something happening.

730
00:45:52,333 --> 00:45:54,583
- What is it?
-  There's a breach.

731
00:45:54,708 --> 00:45:57,582
During the reboot, after the surge,
a connection was made.

732
00:45:57,583 --> 00:46:00,125
Your neural network connected with...

733
00:46:00,292 --> 00:46:03,208
another synth.

734
00:46:08,333 --> 00:46:10,124
Well, that's impossible.

735
00:46:10,125 --> 00:46:12,291
Vision, the connection is still live.

736
00:46:12,292 --> 00:46:15,458
There's something else
still in here. With us.

737
00:46:21,375 --> 00:46:22,542
Is that rain?

738
00:46:23,917 --> 00:46:24,917
No.

739
00:46:25,583 --> 00:46:26,750
Wings.

740
00:46:58,333 --> 00:46:59,333
Hello.

741
00:47:01,250 --> 00:47:04,041
♪ Oh, Danny boy ♪

742
00:47:04,042 --> 00:47:06,833
♪ The pipes, the pipes are calling ♪

743
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:09,000
V!

744
00:47:18,708 --> 00:47:20,333
Hello, Vision.

